{"availability":"available","full":"andy-diericks/ship-or-slip","name":"ship-or-slip","description":"Every date Microsoft promised, and every date it moved. A running history of Microsoft 365 roadmap slips, ships and cancellations, plus Azure retirements — the history Microsoft's own feeds don't keep.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-06T18:42:03Z","updated":"2026-10-11T05:37:26Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://andy-diericks.github.io/ship-or-slip/","topics":["azure","change-tracker","change-tracking","dashboard","github-pages","m365","microsoft","open-data","react","retirementservices","roadmap","typescript","vite"],"demo":"https://andy-diericks.github.io/ship-or-slip/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:25:46.217Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T07:25:46.217Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T07:25:46.217Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T20:10:19.195Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-11T07:25:46.217Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Every date Microsoft promised, and every date it moved.","Microsoft publishes its roadmap in the present tense. The Microsoft 365 roadmap API tells you the date a feature is promised for right now — and when that date quietly moves from September to December, the September is simply gone. Azure retirement notices work the same way: the date changes in place, and one title in the feed today reads \"AV36 Node Retirement now on September 30, 2027\" without a word about what it used to say.","Ship or Slip keeps yesterday's copy and diffs it. Nothing else does."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/andy-diericks/ship-or-slip/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"c92e037c6ad7f45b93b5d4e09df0b5679e3ebfba7af909d070ddfbcef77b582e","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:19.277Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:19.277Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Eve